  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY-BASED MARINE TURTLE CONSERVATION: PROTECTION AND MONITORING OF LEATHERBACK, GREEN, AND HAWKSBILL TURTLES IN THE WESTERN SOLOMON ISLANDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT COMMUNITY-BASED NESTING BEACH CONSERVATION PROGRAMS FOR LEATHERBACK, GREEN AND HAWKBILL SEA TURTLES. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) CONDUCTING NIGHT FOOT SURVEYS ON ABOUT 10 KM OF NESTING BEACH ON TETEPARE, RENDOVA, AND VANGUNU ISLANDS TO COUNT AND PROTECT NESTS FROM POACHING AND PREDATION (2) IMPLEMENTING TRAINING WORKSHOPS ON SEA TURTLE BIOLOGY AND CONSERVATION TECHNIQUES FOR FIELD TEAMS TO BUILD CONSERVATION CAPACITY OF RANGERS AND FIELD MONITORS AND 3) CONDUCTING PUBLIC OUTREACH AND EDUCATION ACTIVITIES TO FOSTER GREATER AWARENESS FOR THE STEWARDSHIP AND CONSERVATION OF SEA TURTLE POPULATIONS.</narrative>
  </description>
